-# NativeCapabilities â€” D06-FMT01 only
-
-Original native-only UWP diagnostic, separate from frozen RuntimeDiagnostics0.1.3.0
-and production LegacyForge. Package NativeDiagnostics0.2.1.0; zero capabilities.
-MTA/CoreApplication startup, one HW D3D11CreateDevice attempt, level11_0, adapter
-SOFTWARE flag classification, one CheckFormatSupport(R8G8B8A8_UNORM) call, scoped release, memory policy, atomic JSON evidence.
-PASS requires TEXTURE2D(0x20), SHADER_SAMPLE(0x200), RENDER_TARGET(0x4000).
-MIP(0x1000) is optional and recorded. Failed/invalid query output has no mask or decoded flags.
-No swapchain, render target, render/presentation loop, additional case or fallback.
-
-UI uses a Windows.UI.Popups.MessageDialog posted on the UI dispatcher after the
-case decision; Windows renders it. No app graphics renderer is linked. Dialog
-availability on this Xbox build is UNTESTED; UI failure does not change the case.
-Unknown activation/case rejects before receipt/worker/device dispatch; repeated
-activation cannot start another case. Dismissal does not retry or launch anything.
-
-Build with existing Windows x64 MSVC14.44.35207 UWP libraries, SDK10.0.26100.0,
-PowerShell7 and Python. No dependency download or target execution:
+# NativeCapabilities â€” D06-RES01a only
+
+Diagnostic NativeDiagnostics0.2.2.0, same separate identity as accepted0.2.1.0,
+zero declared capabilities. Future installation updates/replaces that registration
+and may retain stale LocalState. No signing or installation in this phase.
+Accepted D00 RuntimeDiagnostics and production LegacyForge remain separate.
+
+MTA/CoreApplication startup and LegacyForgeNativeDiagnostics.App entry point retained.
+One fixed hardware device,11_0/BGRA_SUPPORT, no WARP/retry; establish non-software
+adapter. Create exactly one1x1 RGBA8 DEFAULT/SHADER_RESOURCE texture, one mip,
+array1, sample count1/quality0, CPU/misc flags0, null initial data and nonnull output.
+S_OK and nonnull texture required, then GetDesc exact comparison of all11 fields.
+S_FALSE is not allocation success. Scoped texture/device/context references release.
+No CheckFormatSupport sweep, initialization/read of undefined contents, graphics
+views, buffers, shaders, clear/draw/copy/map/readback, swapchain or presentation.
+Driver internal allocations exceed nominal4-byte texel storage and cannot be capped.
+
+Build: existing MSVC14.44.35207 UWP store libraries, SDK10.0.26100.0 C++/WinRT,
+PowerShell7 and Python standard library. No downloads or new dependencies.
+From a clean committed checkout:
 
 ```powershell
 pwsh -NoProfile -File .\diagnostics\NativeCapabilities\build.ps1
 ```
 
-Only committed clean source builds; every build has a new ignored out directory.
-No switches accept runtimes/Java inputs. Native-only macros are fixed and checked.
-The script compiles/preprocesses only app.cpp/report.cpp/probe.cpp and produces
-an unsigned APPX with static audit. Never run the resulting EXE as a smoke test.
-
-10s monotonic case deadline; owner observation30s. Observer cannot cancel a blocked
-GPU or storage call. First terminal decision wins; late PASS is denied. A checkpoint
-may be the only saved evidence after crash/hang. UI saved status is separate from
-in-memory outcome; final JSON has VERIFY_BY_RETRIEVAL rather than predicting flush
-success. Downloaded original and member-hash oracle establish persistence later.
-
-Memory uses observed AppMemoryUsage/Limit: require256MiB headroom before GPU call,
-fail if post-release observed growth exceeds64MiB. Driver allocations cannot be
-strictly capped by this API; no explicit test texture/buffer is allocated. Receipt
-size capped128KiB. Unsupported policy/API becomes BLOCKED with HRESULT. D06-FMT01
-PASS is not all D06, resource-limit, rendering, audio, input, JNI or Minecraft PASS.
-
-No signing, certificate change, deployment, installation, console access or app
-execution is part of this implementation authorization. See the external research
-dossier docs/research/phase-6b5-d06-fmt01 for review and separately gated hardware plan.
-
-API references:
-https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/d3d11/nf-d3d11-d3d11createdevice
-https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/uwp/api/windows.ui.popups.messagedialog?view=winrt-26100
-https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/uwp/gaming/about-the-uwp-user-interface-and-directx
-
-This 0.2.1.0 package shares NativeDiagnostics identity with accepted 0.2.0.0.
-A later installation replaces that registration and may retain LocalState. It
-cannot provide side-by-side HW01 reproduction. If that is required, separately
-approve a distinct package name (for example NativeFormatDiagnostics), isolated
-LocalState and fresh identity evidence before installation. No installed app is
-changed by this build. D00 RuntimeDiagnostics remains a different identity.
-
-Receipt schema v2; tools/receipt_contract.py validates structure/semantics offline.
-Synthetic oracle fixtures are not packaged or represented as Xbox observations.
-CheckFormatSupport docs: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/d3d11/nf-d3d11-id3d11device-checkformatsupport
-Support flag docs: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/d3d11/ne-d3d11-d3d11_format_support
+Fresh ignored build directory, x64 executable and unsigned APPX. Only app.cpp,
+report.cpp and probe.cpp compiled; all preprocessed for Java exclusion. Six unsafe
+macro configurations rejected by compiler. One RES01a case per build; previous
+HW01/FMT01 macros/activation arguments blocked. No runtime file/Java input options.
+
+Receipt schema v3. tools/receipt_contract.py validates structures and case semantics
+with original synthetic JSON fixtures; it never executes target code. Six payload
+roles bound to source/build and current-run UUID. Typical sequence STARTED1 ->
+BEFORE_CREATE_DEVICE2 -> BEFORE_CREATE_TEXTURE3 -> FINAL4. Saved final original,
+independent payload hashes and owner photo/run match required for acceptance.
+NOT EXECUTED is distinct from PASS/FAILED/BLOCKED/INCONCLUSIVE.
+
+10s observational deadline;30s owner window. Watchdog cannot cancel GPU or file calls.
+Initial package hashing/writing precedes timer arming.128KiB per receipt,100ms lock
+acquisition, temp/flush/atomic replace; OS file operations are not hard-time-bounded.
+First terminal wins; late PASS denied. Receipt marker VERIFY_BY_RETRIEVAL is not a
+self-prediction of flush success. Platform MessageDialog is not app rendering.
+Memory policy:>=256MiB before headroom,<=64MiB observed growth; not peak/leak proof.
+
+See external docs/research/phase-6b5-d06-res01a for complete evidence and independently
+gated hardware plan. Never execute the diagnostic as part of a host build check.
+https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/d3d11/nf-d3d11-id3d11device-createtexture2d
